  ),
  title   = "Discovering Regulated Metabolite Families in Untargeted Metabolomics Studies",
  journal = "Analytical Chemistry",
  year    = "2016",
  volume  = "88",
  number  = "16",
  pages   = "8082--8090",
  doi     = "10.1021/acs.analchem.6b01569",
  url     = "https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.analchem.6b01569",
  note    = "PMID: 27452369",
  abstract = paste(
    "The identification of metabolites by mass spectrometry constitutes a major bottleneck",
    "which considerably limits the throughput of metabolomics studies in biomedical or",
    "plant research. Here, we present a novel approach to analyze metabolomics data from",
    "untargeted, data-independent LC-MS/MS measurements. By integrated analysis of MS1",
    "abundances and MS/MS spectra, the identification of regulated metabolite families is",
    "achieved. This approach offers a global view on metabolic regulation in comparative",
    "metabolomics. We implemented our approach in the web application 'MetFamily', which is",
    "freely available. MetFamily provides a dynamic link between MS1-signal intensity patterns",
    "and structural similarity at the MS/MS level. Structurally related metabolites are",
    "annotated as metabolite families based on hierarchical clustering of MS/MS spectra."
  )
